# Public site block for Grafana, imported by the base Caddyfile — only
# mounted when docker-compose.observability.yml is in use (it sets
# GRAFANA_SITE_ADDRESS on the caddy service and mounts this file into
# /etc/caddy/sites-enabled/). Same automatic Let's Encrypt handling as the
# main site: Caddy requests and renews its own certificate for this domain
# too, independently.
#
# No basic auth in front of this on purpose (Logan's call) — Grafana's own
# login (GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD, GF_USERS_ALLOW_SIGN_UP=false) is the
# only gate. Revisit if that ever feels insufficient.
#
# Two blocks, so this file works unmodified whether GRAFANA_SITE_ADDRESS is
# reached via plain DNS (the first block, Caddy's automatic HTTPS) or via
# docker-compose.tunnel.yml's Cloudflare Tunnel (the second): its address is
# explicitly `http://` — a bare `:8080` isn't enough to reliably opt out of
# automatic HTTPS here, since the same hostname also appears in this file's
# other, TLS-managed address; the explicit scheme is Caddy's own documented
# way to force plain HTTP regardless (a bare `hostname:8080` address here
# made Caddy reset the connection instead of serving plain HTTP through it —
# seen live on the VPS via cloudflared's "read: connection reset by peer"
# errors). `:8080` is matched by the Host header cloudflared forwards — see
# docker-compose.tunnel.yml's own comment. Self-hosters without the tunnel
# add-on simply never send traffic to `:8080` — it's not published to the
# host, so nothing outside the compose network can reach it anyway.
#
# Two separate blocks (not one block with two addresses) so the `header_up`
# override below applies only to the tunnel path: Caddy sets
# X-Forwarded-Proto from its own listener's scheme, which is plain http for
# this internal, un-TLS'd hop — even though the original browser connection
# was https all the way to Cloudflare's edge. Without this override, Grafana
# sees an apparently-insecure request behind a `root_url` declared as
# https://…, which breaks secure-cookie/OAuth-callback handling.
{$GRAFANA_SITE_ADDRESS} {
	reverse_proxy grafana:3000
}

http://{$GRAFANA_SITE_ADDRESS}:8080 {
	reverse_proxy grafana:3000 {
		header_up X-Forwarded-Proto https
	}
}
